{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1130","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1130","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1130\",\"parent_revision\":\"a8dda5dbe67e1ef2e3ccd5374242ea1c46a159be1509353c047743322389c739\",\"root_revision\":\"a8dda5dbe67e1ef2e3ccd5374242ea1c46a159be1509353c047743322389c739\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe `dh:discovery` skill (SAM S1) exists and produces a structured DISCOVERY artifact covering WHO/WHAT/WHEN/WHY, goals, anti-goals, NFRs, references, and resolved questions via an interactive confirmation loop. It is not called by any pipeline entry point.\\n\\n**What is broken:**\\n- `create-backlog-item` has no discovery gate \u2014 items are created with thin descriptions and no structured requirements gathering\\n- `groom-backlog-item` proceeds without checking whether discovery has been performed\\n- `work-backlog-item` delegates directly to `feature-researcher` which re-derives WHO/WHAT/WHEN/WHY from the thin backlog item, without an interactive confirmation loop\\n- No entry point checks for a \\\"user-discovery-performed\\\" flag or equivalent artifact\\n- `DISCOVERY.md` and `PLAN.md` are produced as files on disk \u2014 they should be read and written via `artifact_register`/`artifact_read` so they are accessible from worktree-isolated agents and persist across sessions\\n\\n**Desired behavior:**\\n1. At each entry point (`create-backlog-item`, `groom-backlog-item`, `work-backlog-item`), check whether a discovery artifact exists for the item via `artifact_list(issue_number, artifact_type=\\\"feature-context\\\")` or a dedicated discovery artifact type\\n2. If no discovery artifact exists AND item type is not \\\"fix\\\" \u2192 invoke `dh:discovery` before proceeding\\n3. If item type is \\\"fix\\\" \u2192 discovery is optional; proceed without it if not present\\n4. Discovery supports two modes: (a) user-interview seeded then automated, (b) fully automated from existing description\\n5. After discovery completes, planning and research phases run against the discovery dataset, not the raw backlog item description\\n6. `DISCOVERY.md` and `PLAN.md` are written via `artifact_register` and read via `artifact_read`, consistent with how `architect-{slug}.md` and `feature-context-{slug}.md` are already handled\\n\\n**Verbatim user report:** if create,groom,work backlog-item get called and there's no existing flag like \\\"user-discovery-performed\\\" then it should be invoked, to build up the details that user wants in the feature. If its a fix instead of a feature discovery is optional for the user. Then when the discovery stage is done, whether its user interview seeded then automated, or just automated, the planning and research steps should run against that discovery data set. The PLAN.md and DISCOVERY.md do not need to be created as files, but instead get both read and written directly via the backlog mcp artifact system.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: MCP-only pipeline: skills must not read/write local files for backlog or planning data\\nGoal: Replace all local-file reads/writes for backlog/planning data in skill entry points with MCP tool calls, and wire a discovery gate into create/groom/work-backlog-item.\\nConditions:\\n1. work-backlog-item reference files read per-item files from ~/.dh/backlog/ instead of backlog_view | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed step-procedures.md and close-resolve-procedure.md have residual file reads\\n2. discovery/SKILL.md writes .planning/harness/DISCOVERY.md to disk | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: confirmed by impact-analyst\\n3. planning/SKILL.md reads/writes .planning/harness/PLAN.md on disk | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: confirmed by impact-analyst\\n4. MCP artifact tools (artifact_register, artifact_read, artifact_list) exist in server.py | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker confirmed all 4 tools present in server.py\\n5. architect-{slug}.md and feature-context-{slug}.md already use artifact system | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE (partially) | Citation: artifact_register called post-write; filesystem fallback still present in add-new-feature delegation prompts\\n6. dh:discovery skill exists and produces structured artifact | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: confirmed by impact-analyst\\n7. backlog_view returns all detailed fields (description, source, etc.) from GitHub | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE (scoped) | Citation: fact-checker found description/source come from local cache (parsing.py:830-832), but skills calling backlog_view via MCP satisfy the pipeline mandate; server owns cache management\\n8. Entry point skills to modify: create-backlog-item, groom-backlog-item, work-backlog-item | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: confirmed by impact-analyst; discovery gates absent in groom and work-backlog-item\\n9. Discovery gate check via artifact_list | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: artifact_list exists in server.py\\n10. (new) SAM YAML plan routing: ~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/*.yaml content must be accessed via sam_read/sam_list, not artifact_read | Status: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst confirmed sam_read/sam_list MCP tools exist and are the correct interface\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (all artifact tools confirmed present)\\n- Condition 7: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (scoped \u2014 MCP call satisfies mandate regardless of server cache internals)\\n- Condition 10: (new) SAM YAML routing gap identified by impact-analyst\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **wire discovery skill into create/groom/work-backlog-item entry points with artifact-backed discovery.md and plan.md** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User \u2014 design intent from original docs, never connected to entry points\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n- [ ] MEDIUM: add-new-feature/SKILL.md artifact_register calls in Phases 1, 2, 3 are missing `content=` parameter \u2014 worktree-isolated agents will fail to find artifacts via artifact_read (reported by qg-T1-code-reviewer on P1131/T1)\\n- [ ] LOW: artifact-conventions.md File Naming Conventions section still shows stale names (discovery-{slug}.md, plan-{slug}.md) instead of feature-context-{slug}.md and architect-{slug}.md (reported by qg-T1-code-reviewer on P1131/T1)\\n- [ ] PRE-EXISTING: default-development-flow.md line 117 still contains .planning/harness/ reference \u2014 not in current scope, add to backlog (reported by qg-T1-code-reviewer on P1131/T1)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n## Sam Plan Content Github Persistence Code Change Done\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [x] `_try_register_task_plan_artifact` in `sam_schema/server.py` calls `provider.store_artifact_content(...)` after `set_manifest` so plan YAML content is uploaded to the GitHub issue comment on `sam_create`\\n- [x] Upload failure catches `BacklogError | OSError` narrowly, logs a warning, and does not abort registration\\n- [x] Worktree-isolated agents calling `artifact_read(issue_number, \\\"task-plan\\\")` now receive content from GitHub first (local fallback preserved)\\n- [x] Lint passes on `sam_schema/server.py`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Skill File Content Changes Mcp Only Access Skill Edits Todo\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `skills/discovery/SKILL.md` \u2014 replace Write(.planning/harness/DISCOVERY.md) with artifact_register call\\n- [ ] `skills/planning/SKILL.md` \u2014 replace Read/Write(.planning/harness/PLAN.md) with artifact_read/artifact_register\\n- [ ] `skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` \u2014 replace .planning/harness/tasks/ file reads with sam_read/sam_list\\n- [ ] `skills/execution/SKILL.md` \u2014 replace .planning/harness/tasks/ file reads with sam_read\\n- [ ] `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` \u2014 replace 3 .planning/harness/ file reads with artifact_read\\n- [ ] `skills/final-verification/SKILL.md` \u2014 replace DISCOVERY.md and PLAN.md file reads with artifact_read\\n- [ ] `skills/context-integration/SKILL.md` \u2014 replace PLAN.md read/write with artifact_read/artifact_register\\n- [ ] `skills/work-backlog-item/references/close-resolve-procedure.md` \u2014 replace ~/.dh/backlog/ filesystem scan with backlog_view MCP calls\\n- [ ] `skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` \u2014 replace per-item file reads with backlog_view\\n- [ ] `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 remove dh_paths.plan_dir() filesystem fallback from delegation prompts\\n</div>\\n\\n## Stale References Content Updates Todo\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `skills/development-harness/references/artifact-conventions.md` \u2014 update .planning/harness/ storage references to reflect artifact system\\n- [ ] `skills/development-harness/references/sdlc-stage-taxonomy.md` \u2014 artifact_path fields: replace filesystem paths with artifact_read call patterns\\n</div>\\n\\n## Discovery Gate Skill Edits Todo\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `skills/groom-backlog-item` \u2014 add artifact_list(issue_number, artifact_type=\\\"feature-context\\\") check before spawning swarm; invoke dh:discovery if absent and item type is not fix\\n- [ ] `skills/work-backlog-item` \u2014 add same discovery gate before invoking add-new-feature\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n### Skills \u2014 Direct Breaks (9 files)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/discovery/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/planning/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/execution/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/final-verification/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/context-integration/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/close-resolve-procedure.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md`\\n\\n### Skills \u2014 Will Become Inaccurate (5 files)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/sam-definition.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/artifact-conventions.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/sdlc-stage-taxonomy.md`\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md`\\n\\n### Entry Points \u2014 Missing Discovery Gates\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md`\\n\\n### Backend Code\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py`\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\nNo blocking dependencies. All required MCP tools (`artifact_register`, `artifact_list`, `artifact_get`, `artifact_read`, `backlog_view`, `sam_read`, `sam_list`) are confirmed present in `backlog_core/server.py`.\\n\\nOne policy decision must be resolved before `server.py` changes begin: whether `artifact_read` filesystem fallback is removed (strict MCP-only) or retained with a deprecation warning. This is a product decision, not a code dependency. Skill content updates can proceed in parallel.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Size**: L\\n\\n**Breakdown**:\\n- 9 skill/reference files with direct breaking changes (Input/Output section rewrites)\\n- 5 skill/reference files with accuracy drift (targeted content updates)\\n- 1 documentation file (node contract updates)\\n- 2 entry-point skills (discovery gate additions \u2014 minimal change per file)\\n- 1 backend code file (policy decision + targeted code change)\\n\\nTotal: ~20 files, no new MCP tools needed, no schema changes.\\n\\n**Risk**: Medium\\n- Skills are AI-facing instruction documents \u2014 incorrect migration causes silent behavioral regression (agents continue reading local files and succeed on developer machines where `.planning/harness/` exists, but fail in worktree-isolated agents)\\n- `artifact_read` fallback removal is irreversible; requires verifying all producers have been migrated to content-uploading `artifact_register` calls before fallback is removed\\n- SAM YAML plans (`sam_read`/`sam_list`) are a separate system and must not be conflated with harness artifact files during migration\\n\\n**Estimated changes**: ~200-350 lines across all files (content edits, not additions)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Direct Breaks Will Fail Under Mcp Only Enforcement\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSkills that currently read or write `.planning/harness/` filesystem paths:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/discovery/SKILL.md` \u2014 writes `.planning/harness/DISCOVERY.md`; must use `artifact_register`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/planning/SKILL.md` \u2014 reads `DISCOVERY.md`, writes `PLAN.md` on disk; must use `artifact_read` / `artifact_register`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/task-decomposition/SKILL.md` \u2014 reads `PLAN.md`, writes `TASK-{NNN}.md` files; must use `artifact_read` / `artifact_register`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/execution/SKILL.md` \u2014 reads task file from `.planning/harness/tasks/`; must use `artifact_read`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` \u2014 reads `.planning/harness/executions/`, `PLAN.md`, and `tasks/`; all three inputs must use `artifact_read`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/final-verification/SKILL.md` \u2014 reads `DISCOVERY.md` and `PLAN.md`; must use `artifact_read`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/context-integration/SKILL.md` \u2014 reads and writes `PLAN.md`; must use `artifact_read` / `artifact_register`\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/close-resolve-procedure.md` \u2014 Step 9a scans `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/` directly; must use `backlog_view` result only\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` \u2014 lines 163, 301, 346 read per-item files from `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/`; must use `backlog_view` MCP response fields\\n</div>\\n\\n## Will Become Inaccurate Stale Content\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` line 212 \u2014 references \\\"groomed item file\\\" instead of `backlog_view` response `sections` dict\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Phase 3 and Phase 4 delegation prompts include `dh_paths.plan_dir()` filesystem fallback paths alongside `artifact_read` primary path\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/artifact-conventions.md` \u2014 entire document describes `.planning/harness/` as storage convention; must be updated to describe MCP artifact manifest as primary\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/sdlc-stage-taxonomy.md` \u2014 all `artifact_path` fields reference `.planning/harness/` paths; must map to MCP artifact types\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/sam-definition.md` line 71 \u2014 documents `.planning/harness/` as storage location\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 node contracts reference `task_file_path` and `~/.dh/` filesystem paths\\n</div>\\n\\n## Code Changes Needed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (`artifact_read`) \u2014 has local filesystem fallback; policy decision: remove fallback to enforce MCP-only, or retain with clear deprecation warning\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (`artifact_register`) \u2014 ensure content upload is not optional for SKILL.md-produced artifacts; emit error if content cannot be stored in GitHub\\n</div>\\n\\n## Missing Discovery Gates\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 Step 3 does not call `artifact_list` to surface prior planning artifacts before spawning swarm\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 Step 5 does not call `artifact_list` before triggering `add-new-feature`; prior artifacts are not passed as `prior_artifacts` context\\n</div>\\n\\n## Two Distinct Systems Separate Migration Paths\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `.planning/harness/` artifacts (DISCOVERY.md, PLAN.md, TASK-NNN.md) \u2014 migrate to `artifact_register` / `artifact_read` (GitHub Issue comment storage)\\n2. `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/plan/*.yaml` SAM task plans \u2014 access via `sam_read` / `sam_list`; content is never uploaded to GitHub so `artifact_read` cannot serve these files\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-mcp-only-pipeline.md | current | feature-researcher | 2026-03-30T06:25:18.981185+00:00 |\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/patterns-1130.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-03-30T06:25:22.158834+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-mcp-only-pipeline.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-03-30T06:54:16.584906+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | plan/P1130-mcp-only-pipeline.yaml | current |  | 2026-03-30T07:09:11Z |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e9b7858a3c852a4dfdbabe33373a9abe5180445d3bb779bad0ef2daee124be3c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWR_cA\"}"}